  "note": "Independent source rejudgment against the complete RFC 7606 Section 5.1 sender restriction: \"An UPDATE message MUST NOT contain more than one of the following: non-empty Withdrawn Routes field, non-empty Network Layer Reachability Information field, MP_REACH_NLRI attribute, and MP_UNREACH_NLRI attribute.\" Read every tag, including the functional file and EoR test. The 16-combination matrix counts all four fields exactly, including MP attributes independently of NLRI contents. Parsed and wire splitters are forced by mixed shape while the input fits; their outputs assert at most one field and preservation of the announcements/withdrawals. Forwarding checks both matching and different contexts, export override checks two independently preserved fields, and compliant controls assert identity. The degenerate-empty-MP_UNREACH test also forbids a manufactured EoR while retaining all withdrawals. The functional test asserts a complete withdrawal-only wire frame, followed by the announcement, through the parsed daemon relay; it does not prove the zero-copy branch or every combination. NLRIBearingFieldCount's current exhaustive-ignore directive leaves its two MP cases unchanged. Receiver acceptance of old mixed senders remains distinct from the sender split. Verdict enforced. No test or gate execution was performed.",
